  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule now exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-7867f0fc Web logs overview\"**\n- Link: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-7867f0fc-web-logs-overview-24d0dec9a879\n- Four panels: total requests (count), unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`), requests over time (date histogram of `@timestamp`), and requests by response code (`response.keyword`).\n- Time range is set to 2026-10-01 through 2026-12-31 because the sample data sits in that window. Today is 2026-10-12, and the data runs to 2026-12-03, so the default \"last 7 days\" would show nothing.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-7867f0fc 5xx spike\"**\n- Rule ID `8787619f-6b23-4cef-946b-3ebbe8262e04`, type `.es-query`, runs every 1m.\n- Counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` where `response.keyword` is between 500 and 599, over a 5-minute window, and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- No action connector is attached, so the rule will record alerts but won't notify anyone. There are no connectors in this Kibana space.\n\n**Data findings**\n- 14,074 requests total, about 1,001 unique client IPs.\n- Response codes: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), 503 (441). The only 5xx code in the data is 503.\n- Because the sample data is dated in the past and future relative to now, the rule will fire only if new 5xx events arrive in the last 5 minutes. I did not verify that it fires, since there's no live traffic.",
